<Legal
  title="Preview Privacy"
  description="What Volli’s invite-only cloud preview stores, who processes it, and how to request access or deletion."
  path="/legal/privacy/"
>
  <p>
    This page covers the invite-only Volli 0.3 cloud preview and our website and docs.
    Volli is operated by Hussain Phalasiya in Ontario, Canada. For privacy questions or
    requests, reply privately through your preview invitation. Do not post personal data
    or private code in a public issue.
  </p>

  <h2>What the preview handles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account and access:</strong> your name, email, sign-in identity and session
      information from the sign-in service, invitation eligibility, and the version and
      time of your Preview Agreement acceptance.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Workspace data:</strong> Workspace and project details, membership, tickets,
      comments, settings and Session history. History includes prompts, model responses,
      tool calls and results, and agent logs; it can contain source code, file contents,
      paths, personal information or secrets encountered by an agent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connections and stored credentials:</strong> API keys, secrets or integration
      credentials you choose to store with Volli, and connected-account metadata. If you
      connect GitHub, this includes profile, verified email, repository and installation
      information, and authorization tokens. These are separate from subscription logins
      kept on your machine.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service and support data:</strong> device and runner connection information,
      app version, sign-in and security records, service errors, and anything you choose
      to send us for support. Website and service requests expose connection information
      such as IP addresses and browser details to the providers handling them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this data to authenticate you, control preview access, sync your work, operate
    and secure the service, respond to support and privacy requests, and comply with law.
    We do not sell personal data, use your content for advertising, or use it to train AI models.
  </p>

  <h2>Local tools do not mean local history</h2>
  <p>
    In signed-out local mode, your board and Session history are stored on your device.
    Signed-in preview Workspaces and their history sync through our cloud backend. An
    agent running on your Mac can put file contents and command output into that history.
    Treat a synced Session as sensitive as the material it reads. Avoid submitting secrets
    or sensitive or regulated personal data; do not assume redaction catches everything.
  </p>
  <p>
    Model requests go to the model provider or gateway you choose, under your agreement
    with it. When you use a backend-held API connection, Volli's gateway on Cloudflare
    relays requests and responses, including prompts and code context. Subscription
    sign-in credentials and keys kept only on your machine do not pass through that
    gateway. MCP servers, web tools and other services you use can also receive the data
    you or an agent sends them. They have their own privacy practices. Signed-out mode
    does not stop those requests or app update checks.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can receive data</h2>
  <p>
    Our preview subprocessors are <strong>Convex, Cloudflare and WorkOS</strong>. See
    <a href="/legal/subprocessors/">their roles and the data they process</a>. Data may be
    processed outside Canada, including in the United States and on global networks,
    under different laws. We do not promise Canadian-only storage.
  </p>
  <p>
    Other Workspace members can see work shared with them; ticket work is shared by
    default, and Workspace policies can broaden visibility. We may access data as needed
    for support, service operation, security or legal requirements. We may disclose data
    when the law requires it. No system can guarantee perfect security or confidentiality.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional telemetry</h2>
  <p>
    Optional crash reporting and product analytics remain off in this preview unless you
    separately consent. Accepting the Preview Agreement does not opt you in. We will
    update this notice and the provider list before introducing an optional telemetry
    service. Operational records needed to run and secure the service are separate from
    optional telemetry. A telemetry collector you configure yourself receives the events
    you enable for it.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
  <p>
    We retain account and Workspace data to operate the preview unless it is deleted.
    This is not a promise of permanent storage: preview data may be lost or reset.
    Keep your own copies. Settings → Account offers account deletion with a 30-day
    recovery period. You can also ask for access, correction, an export or deletion
    privately through your invitation contact. We may need to verify your identity.
    For shared Workspace content, we may need to involve its owner.
  </p>
  <p>
    Account deletion does not promise that every backup or security record disappears
    at the end of the recovery period. We may retain records for security or legal
    obligations and do not promise a fixed backup purge deadline for this preview.
    Depending on where you live, you may also have rights to object to or restrict
    processing, withdraw consent, or complain to a privacy regulator. These rights are
    not limited by this notice.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will publish an updated version here before materially changing these practices.
    For questions, including how to stop using the preview or exercise your rights,
    contact the person who sent your invitation privately.
  </p>
</Legal>
